WEBVTT

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.240
Come on, Ryo!

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.210
Eat our heads!

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.760
Okay! Here I come!

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.180
Eat up!

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:39.930
So yummy!

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.450
I have an announcement to
make for next week.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:21.820
Classes will be canceled due to renovations.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:27.830
If there's no school next week,
Kirin won't come to visit!

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:30.170
You've all been assigned extra homework instead.

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:32.340
Make sure to complete it.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.290
Okay...

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:36.170
I'll be... all alone!

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.050
What's wrong, Machiko?

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.600
Are you that upset classes are canceled?

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.220
Impressive. Such a model student!

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:47.980
Um, I don't really think that's why she's upset.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:49.140
Ryo!

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:52.810
Did you hear that we have next week off?!

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:54.230
Kirin!

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:58.700
I don't think I can handle not seeing you for two weeks!

00:02:58.700 --> 00:02:59.860
Me too!

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:05.740
I had a full-course Chinese dinner planned too...

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.540
Full... course?!

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.500
W-With dumplings?!

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:14.170
Yep, with dumplings.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:19.920
I was going to make pork potstickers <i>and</i> chewy boiled shrimp dumplings—

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:24.220
Hold it! I'll call my parents and ask if I can still stay over!

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:26.350
<i>Hungry </i>and<i> thirsty.</i>

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:27.850
Hi, Mom?

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:31.350
I have next week off from cram school, but...

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:33.020
Yeah.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:38.400
Instead of just staying home next weekend, can I come down to Tokyo like usual?

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:43.610
What? You wanted to go out for dinner?

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:46.200
To a three-star Chinese restaurant?!

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.200
Let's go!

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.410
Ditched...

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:57.170
Sorry, Ryo. I just can't resist three stars.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.710
It's okay.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:03:59.840
I know!

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.180
You can come over,

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:05.340
and I'll ask Mom if you can come with us!

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:11.140
Oh, no, I couldn't possibly intrude on a family event like that.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:12.310
You sure?

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:22.740
What about you, Shiina?
Do you have any plans for next week?

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.700
You could always come...

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:28.330
What are you wearing?!

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:33.120
I don't deal very well with getting wet.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:36.540
Just a little dampness, and I'm stuck in bed all week.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.920
Just coming to school puts my life at risk.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:41.050
<i>I never realized she was so frail!</i>

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:45.340
If the weather's like this again next week,
I'll probably just stay home and study.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.600
I see. That's too bad.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.600
Well, if I try my best, I might be able to make it.

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:52.810
Really?

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:54.940
If I try, sure.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:58.940
I almost never get wet when I dress up like this.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:06.490
Last week's rain continues to pour down,

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:10.410
with overcast skies expected today, tomorrow, and throughout the weekend.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.160
The west coast stays cloudy...

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:19.170
Expect more rain and even denser cloud coverage on the east coast.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:24.170
<i>So in the end, I ended up all alone.</i>

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:27.680
It's just another rainy Saturday.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:32.930
I wonder if Shiina's feeling any better?

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:38.440
I wonder what Kirin's up to?

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:42.190
Ryo, if you get lonely, just text me!

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:45.530
<i>Hi, Kirin.</i>

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:48.200
<i>Too bad it's still raining. What are you doing?</i>

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.120
And Shiina too.

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:54.540
<i>Hello, Shiina. How are you feeling?</i>

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:18.730
Of course they're not going to respond so soon.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:22.110
This is when you need tasty food the most!

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:26.070
Something simple, to wipe this gloomy mood away!

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:32.910
All done!

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:36.040
Chilled ramen with sesame sauce!

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:39.960
Oh no, because it's Saturday I...

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:45.300
Anyway, let's eat.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:07.860
It's great!

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:13.570
Eating alone is rather dreary, though.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:18.790
Still no reply...

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:22.540
She said that I could text her anytime,

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:27.130
but I guess she didn't say she'd respond.

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:32.390
And look at him, actin' all needy 'cause I didn't text him back!

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:35.100
C'mon, man, you could at least reply.

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:39.480
If you want me to reply, how about you try writing something interesting for once?

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:42.730
Hey, what can I say? I'm bored!

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.400
No way!

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:49.240
I'm definitely not like that!

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:52.360
A text!

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:05.500
I kind of feel bad for making her type all that out when she's sick.

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:10.340
Hi, Kirin.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:15.140
Don't you think this pattern in the ceiling looks like a face?

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:20.600
I don't even know how she'd begin to answer that.

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:24.230
Jeez, what am I doing?

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.070
<i>It's strange.</i>

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:41.750
<i>How </i>did<i> I spend my days off before Kirin began visiting?</i>

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:47.710
This won't do!

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:50.300
I know! I'll study.

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:56.510
I need something else to work with.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:59.470
I know, I'll go check something out from the library.

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:03.730
<i>I knew it.</i>

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:07.480
<i>Being shut up in my house was just making me depressed.</i>

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:11.860
<i>Going outside lets me experience the season.</i>

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:12.780
<i>And...</i>

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:26.790
<i>I'll send Kirin a text I know she'll want to respond to!</i>

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:30.460
Wait a minute! I need to get that book!

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:37.640
<i>I haven't been to the library in a while.</i>

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:38.680
Ryo?!

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:44.060
Ryo!

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:48.940
It's me, Ryo!

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:51.900
Oh, Ms. Watanabe!

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:53.730
You should've heard yourself scream!

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:55.570
Sorry to startle you like that.

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:57.570
Management made me wear this.

00:09:57.570 --> 00:09:59.370
The kids love it!

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.910
Kids like it?

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:03.700
Anyway, Ryo, long time no see.

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:05.830
Yeah, it's been a while.

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:07.460
About five years, right?

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:10.960
You used to come here with your grandma all the time.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:15.670
You've certainly grown into a fine young woman.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:17.760
Oh, don't flatter me...

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:21.640
And now that you're all grown up, I can reveal to you one of the seven wonders of our library:

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:25.020
The "secret door to another world"!

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:26.810
Just kidding.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:27.850
Really?!

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:32.110
<i>She's still the same inside!</i>

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:35.610
Hey, hey, Ms. Watanabe!

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.650
Turn into the Rain-or-Shine Monk again!

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:39.280
It's so cute!

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:40.910
Right away.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:44.910
I-I guess that costume's more popular than I thought.

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:48.660
Anyway, Ms. Watanabe, do you have a moment?

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:54.090
<i>The smell of books is so nostalgic.</i>

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:11.350
<i>I always read children's books while waiting for Grandma to choose hers.</i>

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.440
Over here, Ryo!

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.570
Hm? Oh, thanks.

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:22.450
Are these all cookbooks?

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:26.700
That's right. Your grandma used to borrow them all the time.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.870
She did?

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:32.920
But these are all for beginners...

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:35.920
I remember her well.

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:38.380
When I first began working here,
she came in all teary-eyed, asking

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:43.180
"Where are the books which will make me good at cooking?"

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:45.720
She was so lovable.

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:51.190
Wouldn't that mean she was bad at cooking?

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:52.600
Hm? Wasn't she?

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:55.940
Grandma?

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:58.820
Oh yeah, she was a terrible cook.

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:00.740
Are you serious?!

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:04.320
Didn't I ever tell you?

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:05.370
When my big sister...

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:08.450
Um, when your mom and I were little,

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:11.790
she could barely cook a fish without either burning it or leaving it half-raw.

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:14.460
Her miso soup was like water too.

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:17.090
I swear she forgot to add the stock.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:19.920
The lunches she packed us were terrible too.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:23.590
Just rice with a big glop of red bean paste on top.

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:27.350
It was like some messed up rice candy.

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:34.520
It wasn't until she started looking after you that she got serious about cooking.

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:39.730
She did it for me?

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:49.660
Teriyaki chicken, stir-fried tofu...

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:53.620
Wow, these are all things she used to make!

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.040
Huh?

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:57.000
What is it?

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:01.300
These aren't quite the recipes Grandma taught me.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:05.720
The ones I know have a bit less salt and are a little sweeter.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:10.100
Well, she did say she was modifying them a bit for you.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:16.020
She most likely had your tastes and
preferences in mind while she cooked,

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:19.570
rather than just following the recipes to the book.

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:26.820
She was cooking with love.

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:29.580
I...

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:31.290
It's done.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:32.910
Here you go.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:38.210
I really was raised with such loving food.

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:43.130
My tummy...

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:46.010
It must be because we were talking about food.

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:48.140
Why not have something to eat in the lounge?

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:50.680
You can get lunch at the corner store like you always used to.

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:52.970
That's a great idea!

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:56.690
Wow, it's still the same.

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:03.530
<i>Grandma would always buy our lunches here whenever we went to the library.</i>

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:07.150
<i>I still remember her saying it was a "special treat."</i>

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:14.870
Welcome.

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:18.370
I guess I used to always hide behind her.

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:21.880
This really brings me back.

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:27.720
Welcome.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:30.510
<i>H-He's still here!</i>

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:33.140
<i>And he looks exactly the same!</i>

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:43.860
This was the only time she let me have whatever I wanted.

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:48.820
They still have everything they used to have.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:51.740
It feels like I was just here yesterday.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:55.370
Oh, but there are plenty of new things too!

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:59.920
<i>Chewy bread and cakes.</i>

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.090
<i>Maybe I should get a salted rice ball...</i>

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:07.550
<i>...and have it with something from the deli.</i>

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:10.760
<i>What do I want?</i>

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:17.680
<i>She was just as indecisive back then too.</i>

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:20.190
<i>But man, she's grown up so much...</i>

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.020
Excuse me, do you mind if I...

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:37.040
Welcome back. Did you find anything good?

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:41.250
Yep, and I got pictures too.

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:49.260
<i>I had such a hard time deciding that I ended up just getting the usual:</i>

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.010
<i>A rice ball,</i>

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:53.220
<i>popcorn chicken from the hot bar,</i>

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:54.800
<i>orange juice,</i>

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:58.060
<i>and a cream puff for dessert.</i>

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:02.770
It's pretty much what I always used to get.

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:06.060
Whenever I couldn't decide, I ended up with these.

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:14.320
Grandma always had cup noodles, chips, and a cola.

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:18.740
Now that I think of it, those are some really strange choices.

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:24.330
She must have been picking all the things she couldn't have normally.

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:28.300
Anyway, time to eat!

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:36.550
<i>The soft texture of the tuna,</i>

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:39.140
<i>the steady savoriness of the kelp...</i>

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:42.560
<i>That crunchy texture which you only get from corner store seaweed.</i>

00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:04.120
<i>The addictive, salty, spicy flavor of the soy sauce marinade,</i>

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:07.920
<i>and the fresh juicy chicken underneath the crunchy breading.</i>

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:18.550
<i>The fluffy butter pastry,</i>

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:25.520
<i>filled with a gentle, mildly-sweet custard cream that envelops my entire mouth.</i>

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:31.280
<i>They taste just like how I remember except even better!</i>

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:33.280
Welcome back!

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:36.240
Ah! Not so fast!

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:40.280
You've gotten even tastier since the last time I saw you!

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:42.370
She's digging right in!

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:48.710
<i>In a way, I'm amazed by how much they've grown up since I last saw them.</i>

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:51.960
That was good.

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:57.470
<i>Even though I couldn't really enjoy breakfast,</i>

00:17:57.470 --> 00:18:01.810
<i>just thinking of Grandma while I ate made this meal so tasty.</i>

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:11.400
<i>I never realized just how hard she worked for me.</i>

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:20.910
<i>That must be why the meals she cooked for me always tasted so good.</i>

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:28.420
<i>When cooking, you have to cook for someone close to you.</i>

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:34.170
<i>That might even be the most important part.</i>

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:47.890
<i>Have I ever cooked for someone while thinking of how it will make them feel?</i>

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:51.150
Kirin...

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:54.940
<i>I want to be with Kirin right now.</i>

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:55.650
Delish!

00:18:55.650 --> 00:19:00.780
<i>I want to be with her, cook good food for her,</i>

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:04.790
<i>and see her warm smile.</i>

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:06.620
All right!

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:11.920
I'm going to do what Grandma did, and learn to cook for Kirin!

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:17.840
The first step is to think deeply about her.

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:20.130
Kirin, Kirin...

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:23.050
I love you, Kirin!

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:29.060
What's wrong, Kirin?

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:31.400
Oh, nothing...

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:34.650
I swear I just heard Ryo's voice.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:40.780
No phones at the table, Kirin.

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:42.450
Sec, I'm going to the bathroom.

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:49.790
That kid has terrible manners. Who raised her like that?

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:51.160
Oh yeah, I did.

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:00.010
That was my shrimp...

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:01.680
Sorry, Ryo.

00:20:02.050 --> 00:20:03.800
I've been so busy today that...

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:05.970
Wow, ten texts?!

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:11.810
I didn't realize she needed me around that much!

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:14.940
Wait, some old guy?

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:16.570
What on earth is that?

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:20.070
Wait, is she mad?

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:31.710
I dunno what's going on,
but I think she's enjoying herself.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:39.210
<i>Cooking while imagining her face...</i>

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:48.680
Kirin's having Chinese tonight, so...

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:54.020
How about something Western next week?

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:58.940
Maybe Italian. Pizza with a homemade crust?

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:02.320
On the other hand...

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:07.200
This.

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:14.250
<i>These will make both me </i>and<i> her happy.</i>

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:17.000
Kirin!

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:28.760
My dumplings...

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:33.140
I was right!

00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:36.980
Boiled dumplings, potstickers...

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:41.480
I may even try steaming some.

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:56.960
You'd better make it over next week!

00:23:40.940 --> 00:23:43.810
I don't know what to do!

00:23:43.810 --> 00:23:47.400
It's not like you to look that
depressed at the table, Morino.

00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:48.110
But but but!

00:23:48.110 --> 00:23:50.490
It's really fun to pour them in, so I want to do that,

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:53.450
but scooping them out is fun too!

00:23:53.450 --> 00:23:55.700
I want to focus on eating them too,
but I can't do all three!

00:23:56.530 --> 00:24:00.910
There needs to be three of me, so one can pour, one can scoop, and one can eat!

00:24:00.910 --> 00:24:04.000
Three Morinos is more than I can take.

